Use lowercase psapi.lib so the cross-link resolves on a case-sensitive host.

libslic3r links the Win32 system lib as `Psapi.lib`. lld-link on Linux resolves
library names case-sensitively against the xwin Windows-SDK splat, which ships
`psapi.lib` / `PSAPI.lib` but not the mixed-case `Psapi.lib`, so the link fails
with "could not open 'Psapi.lib'". Lowercase resolves on both the cross host and
native Windows (case-insensitive there), so it's safe everywhere.

Applied to the OrcaSlicer submodule at cross-build time; tree left pinned.

diff --git a/src/libslic3r/CMakeLists.txt b/src/libslic3r/CMakeLists.txt
index 9b67d7ab50..f1ab53b981 100644
--- a/src/libslic3r/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/src/libslic3r/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -625,7 +625,7 @@ if (TARGET OpenVDB::openvdb)
 endif()

 if(WIN32)
-    target_link_libraries(libslic3r PRIVATE Psapi.lib bcrypt.lib)
+    target_link_libraries(libslic3r PRIVATE psapi.lib bcrypt.lib)
 endif()

 if(SLIC3R_PROFILE)
